NOTES=KEY FINDING: the vendor XML declares NO AV1 and lists only OMX.* (so all c2.* Codec2 components are invisible to it) — the API disagreed with the config file. User rule: never rely on config files when you can ask via API. Consequences: H.265 software gap is DESKTOP-ONLY (device has HW); do NOT bundle dav1d for Android. NEXT = M2 step 1: prove the playback contract on DESKTOP with a local VP9/WebM file using the codec we already have (opaque decoded-frame + timestamp-us + present(at-ns) + flush/reset, sync guest-side vs wasi:audio position()). No new codec until that shape is proven. Probe binary on device at /data/local/tmp/wandr-host-probe (needs LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/data/local/tmp).
